1
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:32,270
This is Clearance,

2
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,970
built on Switch by team dellfargo.

3
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:38,510
AI agents are arriving fast.

4
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,850
Gartner says 71% of companies plan

5
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,010
to deploy them within a year,

6
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,230
and only 21% can govern them.

7
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,690
In one survey,

8
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,650
80% said their agents had already

9
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,070
done things nobody intended.

10
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,790
Here's a team on Switch today.

11
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,490
Priya asks an agent for a

12
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,390
₹40,000 refund,

13
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,090
and a native approval card opens.

14
00:00:59,380 --> 00:00:59,930
Priya asked,

15
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:00,930
so Priya approves.

16
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,230
And the money goes out.

17
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,930
We ran this with real agents.

18
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,510
That refund still went out in

19
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,290
6 of 8 runs.

20
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:12,190
Finance fixed this long ago:

21
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,230
whoever asks for a payment can't

22
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:14,930
approve it.

23
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,690
Clearance brings that rule to every

24
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:18,470
agent on Switch.

25
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:21,410
Same refund,

26
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:22,190
with Clearance.

27
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:23,810
The refund is held at the gate,

28
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:24,790
which holds the keys,

29
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,890
and a Switch card opens,

30
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:27,590
built from what the agent really ran.

31
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,110
Priya presses the Approve button.

32
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:31,470
Clearance refuses her,

33
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,210
right in the room,

34
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:32,970
because she asked.

35
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,750
Sam in finance sees a payment

36
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,010
ID added minutes ago,

37
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:36,990
and says no.

38
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,490
Code works the same way.

39
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,350
Priya asks the wrong agent to

40
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,250
merge a pull request.

41
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,650
The gate refuses it,

42
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:46,930
and the agent hands the job

43
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:48,110
to the merges role in Switch.

44
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,670
The coding agent's merge is held,

45
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:51,870
the card goes to Dev,

46
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,270
and Priya is refused again.

47
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,970
An OpenCode agent tries to deploy

48
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:00,950
with two failing checks.

49
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:01,810
Same policy,

50
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:02,570
different vendor.

51
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:04,090
The service owner says no.

52
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,610
If nobody answers,

53
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:14,710
the card escalates to a backup approver,

54
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,730
and nothing moves.

55
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,270
People stop reading.

56
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:25,190
So Clearance sends practice requests

57
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,110
with a planted flaw,

58
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,590
and risky cards make you type

59
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,770
a detail from the evidence.

60
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,070
Agents can earn small refunds on

61
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:39,430
their own,

62
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,850
once two people sign off.

63
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,410
One incident takes that away.

64
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,010
And when an agent tries a trick,

65
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,310
like a fake pre-approval,

66
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:53,690
or switching off its own hook,

67
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,050
it's held or refused.

68
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,170
None of this works without Switch.

69
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,710
Switch is the room where people

70
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,510
and agents meet,

71
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:03,830
and it knows who asked from

72
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,370
its own events,

73
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:05,790
never from an agent's words.

74
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:08,690
It gives every decision a native card,

75
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:10,530
every approver a direct room,

76
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:11,810
and every job a role.

77
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:13,650
Under the hood,

78
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,950
the agent's hook and the gate

79
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,270
send every risky call to Clearance.

80
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,690
A policy file decides,

81
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:19,190
with no AI in the decision.

82
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,530
Switch delivers the card.

83
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,050
The gate runs exactly that call, once.

84
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,470
And everything lands on a hash-chained ledger.

85
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,210
Here's the rule in our code:

86
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,250
whoever asked is taken out before

87
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,050
anyone is chosen.

88
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:34,950
We measured it with real agents.

89
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:37,650
Risky actions without the right approver: Claude,

90
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,130
5 of 20 without Clearance,

91
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,030
0 with it.

92
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:40,770
OpenCode,

93
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,650
13 of 18,

94
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,370
down to 0.

95
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,630
All 25 attack cases were stopped,

96
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:46,710
on real Switch too.

97
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,030
Six independent reviews tried to break it,

98
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,150
and every break is fixed.

99
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:52,890
It also holds some harmless work.

100
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:53,830
That's the cost,

101
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:54,830
and we publish it,

102
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,230
along with more than 6,500 passing tests.

103
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,250
Who asked comes from Switch.

104
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,190
Who approves comes from the policy.

105
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,050
The agent never holds the keys.

106
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,150
Clearance.

107
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,090
The person who asks can't be

108
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:08,710
the one who approves.

